-- title:
--   Weighted Pólya enumeration with the group factor retained
-- statement:
--   Let a finite group $G$ act on a finite set of positions $D$. Let $C$ be a finite set of colors, $R$ a commutative ring, and $w:C\to R$ a weight function. The induced action on colorings is $(g\cdot f)(d)=f(g^{-1}\cdot d)$. For each orbit $O$ of colorings under the full group, define $W(O)=\prod_{d\in D}w(f(d))$ using any representative $f$. For $g\in G$, let $\mathcal C_g$ be the orbits of positions under the cyclic subgroup generated by $g$, and write $|\sigma|$ for an orbit's cardinality. Then in $R$,
--
--   $$(|G|\cdot1_R)\sum_{O\in(D\to C)/G}W(O)
--   =\sum_{g\in G}\prod_{\sigma\in\mathcal C_g}\left(\sum_{c\in C}w(c)^{|\sigma|}\right).$$
--
--   All sums and products are finite. This connects weights of coloring orbits to the cyclic orbit structure of each group element, without assuming that the scalar $|G|\cdot1_R$ is invertible.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/xiangyazi24/AnalyticCombinatorics/blob/f6f3f1cebdae245a61d9d71e6b47c69fbd096fe3/AnalyticCombinatorics/Ch1/Polya/Weighted.lean#L251
